{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Nakayama's Lemma.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Nakayama's Lemma.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"nakayama s lemma nakayama s lemma","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Nakayama's Lemma.md","fileName":"Nakayama's Lemma.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Nakayama's Lemma","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 19:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Module Structure and Exact Sequences]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Module Structure and Exact Sequences","Jacobson Radical","Local Ring","Residue Field","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Nakayama's Lemma.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Nakayama's Lemma.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"nakayama s lemma nakayama s lemma","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Nakayama's Lemma.md","fileName":"Nakayama's Lemma.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Nakayama's Lemma","heading":"Nakayama's Lemma","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Nakayama's lemma states that if M is a finitely generated module and I lies in the [[Jacobson Radical]], then IM = M implies M = 0. More generally, M = IM + N implies M = N.\n\nOver a [[Local Ring]], a basis of M/mM over the [[Residue Field]] lifts to a minimal generating set of M. The lemma converts information after reduction modulo the maximal ideal into information about the original module.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Module Structure and Exact Sequences","Jacobson Radical","Local Ring","Residue Field","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Nakayama's Lemma.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Nakayama's Lemma.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"nakayama s lemma nakayama s lemma","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Nakayama's Lem